#: includes/help.php:32
msgid "Distinct people over the period, recognised by a pseudonymous fingerprint that resets every night. Someone who comes back tomorrow counts as a new visitor: compare trends rather than absolute numbers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:33
msgid "A sequence of pages viewed by the same visitor with less than 30 minutes of inactivity between them. One person can make several visits in a day."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:34
msgid "Every page displayed. A page reloaded, or seen twice during the same visit, counts twice."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:35
msgid "Paid WooCommerce orders over the period, refunds deducted. Read from your store whatever the origin of the order — orders created by hand or imported are included."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:36
#: includes/query.php:220
#: views/acquisition.php:29
#: views/ecommerce.php:32
#: views/overview.php:100
msgid "Conversion rate"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:36
msgid "Share of measured visits that ended in a paid order. Only orders linked to a measured visit count, which keeps the rate honest: orders placed by hand or before tracking started are left out."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:37
#: includes/query.php:221
#: views/acquisition.php:30
#: views/acquisition.php:60
#: views/ecommerce.php:31
msgid "Average basket"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:37
msgid "Revenue divided by the number of orders. A rising basket with fewer orders can hide a drop in volume: read both together."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:38
msgid "Paid WooCommerce orders over the period. Cancelled and failed orders are excluded; refunded ones are deducted from revenue."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:39
#: views/comportement.php:27
#: views/overview.php:101
#: views/visiteurs.php:33
msgid "Bounce rate"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:39
msgid "Share of visits that viewed a single page. Normal on a blog post; on a product or landing page it usually means the page did not match what the visitor expected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:40
#: views/comportement.php:26
#: views/overview.php:103
#: views/visites.php:212
#: views/visiteurs.php:31
msgid "Average duration"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:40
msgid "Average time actually spent on pages, counted only while the tab is active. Time spent in a background tab is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:41
#: views/ecommerce.php:33
#: views/overview.php:102
msgid "Value per visit"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:41
msgid "Revenue divided by visits: what one visit is worth on average. Handy to compare traffic sources of very different sizes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:42
#: views/ecommerce.php:34
msgid "Attributed revenue"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:42
msgid "Part of the revenue that a measured visit explains. The rest comes from orders placed before tracking started, offline, by hand, or by visitors who block scripts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:43
#: views/comportement.php:25
#: views/visites.php:208
#: views/visiteurs.php:32
msgid "Pages per visit"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:43
msgid "Page views divided by visits — the depth of browsing. Below 1.5 on a shop, most visitors leave from the page they landed on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:44
#: views/visiteurs.php:30
msgid "Visits per visitor"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:44
msgid "Visits divided by visitors, within the same day: the fingerprint that recognises a visitor resets every night."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:45
#: views/ecommerce.php:50
#: views/overview.php:89
msgid "Conversion funnel"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:45
msgid "The four steps of a purchase: visit, add to cart, order started, paid order. Each percentage is read from the first step; the loss between two steps shows where visitors give up."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:46
#: views/ecommerce.php:60
msgid "Vanishing points"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:46
msgid "Visits lost between two consecutive steps of the funnel. The biggest gap is the first place to look."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:47
msgid "Traffic sources"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:47
msgid "Where visits come from: the referring site, a UTM tag or a campaign link. “Direct” means no referrer — bookmarks, typed addresses, some apps and e-mail clients."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:48
#: views/acquisition.php:114
msgid "Referring sites"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:48
msgid "Third-party sites whose links brought visitors, search engines and social networks aside."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:49
#: views/acquisition.php:90
msgid "Revenue by channel"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:49
msgid "Revenue of the orders linked to a visit from each source. Orders without a measured visit do not appear here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:50
#: views/acquisition.php:101
msgid "Conversion by channel"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:50
msgid "Conversion rate of each source. A small source with a high rate is often worth more attention than a large one that never converts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:51
#: views/comportement.php:13
msgid "Entry pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:51
msgid "First page of each visit. An entry page that performs poorly loses visitors before they see anything else."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:52
#: views/comportement.php:14
msgid "Exit pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:52
msgid "Last page of each visit. Every visit ends somewhere: an exit page is only a problem when it is not the natural end of a journey."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:53
#: views/comportement.php:15
msgid "Internal searches"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:53
msgid "Terms typed into your store’s search box. What people look for without finding often says more than a ranking of pages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:54
msgid "Visitor paths"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:54
msgid "The most frequent sequences of pages, step by step, from a chosen starting page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:55
msgid "Product views"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:55
msgid "Product pages displayed, the visitors who saw them, and the share that added the product to the cart."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:56
msgid "Add-to-cart rate"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:56
msgid "Add-to-cart events divided by product views. Low on a heavily viewed product, it usually points at the price, the photos, the stock or the delivery information."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:57
msgid "Countries"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:57
msgid "Read from a header sent by your host or CDN, from WooCommerce geolocation when enabled, or from the browser language as a last resort. Never stored together with an address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:58
#: views/comportement.php:17
#: views/comportement.php:59
#: views/temps-reel.php:92
#: views/visiteurs.php:55
msgid "Devices"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:58
msgid "Mobile, tablet or desktop, deduced from the browser signature."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:59
msgid "New or returning"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:59
msgid "“Returning” means already seen earlier the same day, since the fingerprint resets every night. It is not a customer loyalty metric."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:60
#: views/visiteurs.php:111
msgid "Screen resolutions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:60
msgid "Width × height of the visitors’ screens. Test the store first on the most frequent ones."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:61
msgid "Visits active over the last 30 minutes, refreshed every 20 seconds. Useful during a campaign launch or a newsletter send."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:62
#: views/campagnes.php:74
msgid "Campaign revenue"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:62
msgid "Net revenue of the orders linked to a tagged visit, refunds deducted, within the attribution window set in Settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:63
#: views/campagnes.php:75
msgid "Invested"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:63
msgid "Sum of the budgets entered on the campaign sheets. Without a budget, no return can be computed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:64
msgid "Return"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:64
msgid "Revenue divided by budget: euros earned per euro spent. Below 1, the campaign cost more than it brought in — and this is before your margin."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %1$s: conversion rate.
#: includes/help.php:65
#: views/campagne.php:91
msgid "Cost per order"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:65
msgid "Budget divided by attributed orders. Compare it with your margin on an average order."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:66
#: views/campagne.php:114
msgid "Attributed orders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:66
msgid "Orders whose visit carried this campaign, within the attribution window."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:67
#: views/campagne.php:96
msgid "Objective"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:67
msgid "Revenue target entered on the campaign sheet, compared with the net revenue actually attributed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:68
#: views/produits.php:35
msgid "References sold"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:68
msgid "Distinct products with at least one paid order over the period."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:69
#: views/produits.php:36
msgid "Items sold"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:69
msgid "Units sold over the period, refunded units deducted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:70
msgid "Products revenue"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:70
msgid "Revenue of the product lines, shipping and taxes aside. It can differ slightly from the store revenue for that reason."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:71
#: views/produits.php:38
msgid "Average price"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:71
msgid "Products revenue divided by units sold: the price actually paid per unit, promotions included."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:72
#: views/visites.php:203
msgid "Routes displayed"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:72
msgid "The visits listed below, taken among the most recent of the period and of the chosen segment. The statistics on this line describe this group only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php:73
#: views/visites.php:216
