#: includes/insights.php:124
msgid "Conversion fell while traffic held"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:125
msgid "About as many visits as during the previous period, but noticeably fewer of them ended in an order. That points at the store rather than at the traffic: a checkout change, a stock or delivery issue, a price move, a technical error on a device."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: current conversion rate, 2: previous conversion rate, 3: traffic change in percent.
#: includes/insights.php:127
#, php-format
msgid "Conversion %1$s vs %2$s before · visits %3$s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:128
msgid "Place a test order on mobile and desktop, then check the funnel screen for the step that lost the most."
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:132
msgid "Traffic dropped sharply"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:133
msgid "A quarter fewer visits than during the previous period. Before worrying, check whether the previous period included a campaign, a newsletter or a seasonal peak — a drop after a peak is not a decline."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: current visits, 2: previous visits.
#: includes/insights.php:135
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s visits vs %2$s before"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:136
msgid "Compare the sources on the Acquisition screen with the previous period to see which one fell."
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:147
msgid "Half of the orders have no measured visit"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:148
msgid "Conversion rates and campaign figures only see orders linked to a visit. Orders created by hand, imported, placed by an excluded role, or by visitors who block scripts stay invisible to them — without being lost for the store."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: orders linked to a visit, 2: total orders.
#: includes/insights.php:150
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s of %2$s orders linked to a visit"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:151
msgid "If most orders come from the site itself, check the excluded roles and paths in Settings, and whether a cache or consent tool blocks the tracking script."
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:168
msgid "Mobile converts much less than desktop"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:169
msgid "A gap is normal — people browse on the phone and buy on the computer — but a rate below half of the desktop one often hides a practical obstacle: a form that is hard to fill, a payment method missing on mobile, a slow page, a popup covering the button."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: mobile conversion rate, 2: desktop conversion rate, 3: mobile visits.
#: includes/insights.php:171
#, php-format
msgid "Mobile %1$s vs desktop %2$s, over %3$s mobile visits"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:172
msgid "Go through the whole purchase on a real phone, from the product page to the payment confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:185
msgid "Most carts are abandoned"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:186
msgid "Fewer than three carts out of ten turn into an order. The usual suspects: delivery costs discovered late, a mandatory account, a long form, a doubt about the return policy. It can also be visitors comparing prices — carts are not commitments."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: add-to-cart count, 2: paid orders.
#: includes/insights.php:188
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s carts · %2$s paid orders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:189
msgid "Show delivery costs and delays before the cart, and allow ordering without an account."
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:193
msgid "Half of the started orders never complete"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:194
msgid "Visitors who reach the checkout have decided to buy; losing one in two there points at the checkout itself: a payment method that fails, an error message, a field that rejects a valid address."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: started checkouts, 2: paid orders.
#: includes/insights.php:196
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s checkouts started · %2$s paid orders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:197
msgid "Check the failed and pending orders in WooCommerce for a repeated payment error."
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:217
msgid "An entry page loses most of its visitors at once"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:218
msgid "Visitors who land on this page leave without viewing anything else, far more often than elsewhere on the store. Either the page does not match what brought them there, or something is wrong with it — loading time, layout on mobile, missing call to action."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: page path, 2: bounce rate, 3: number of entries.
#: includes/insights.php:220
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s · %2$s bounce over %3$s entries"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:221
msgid "Open the page from the source that sends the most visitors to it, and read it as they would."
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:245
msgid "A busy source never converts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:246
msgid "Plenty of visits, not a single order, while the store converts elsewhere. Either the visitors it sends are not looking for what you sell, or they land on a page that does not lead to the catalogue. If you pay for this traffic, this is where the money goes first."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: source label, 2: number of visits.
#. translators: 1: country name, 2: number of visits.
#: includes/insights.php:248
#: includes/insights.php:316
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s · %2$s visits · 0 orders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:249
msgid "Look at the entry pages of this source on the Journeys screen, then at what these visitors do next."
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:255
msgid "One source converts far better than the rest"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:256
msgid "Its visitors buy much more often than average. That is usually a sign of a good match between the audience and the offer — and an argument for sending more of them, if the source can scale."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: source label, 2: conversion rate, 3: store conversion rate.
#: includes/insights.php:258
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s · %2$s conversion vs %3$s for the store"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:259
msgid "Check whether the volume can grow before drawing conclusions: a small, well-targeted source rarely stays that efficient when it is scaled up."
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:286
msgid "A popular product is almost never added to the cart"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:287
msgid "Many visitors look at it, very few take the next step, far below what your other products achieve. The page itself is the first suspect: price, photos, description, stock message, delivery information, or a variation that cannot be selected."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: product name, 2: views, 3: add-to-cart count.
#: includes/insights.php:289
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s · %2$s views · %3$s added to cart"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:290
msgid "Open the product page on a phone and try to add it to the cart, variation included."
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:299
msgid "Visitors keep searching for the same thing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:300
msgid "A term typed again and again in the search box is a demand expressed in the visitors’ own words. If you sell it, make it easier to find; if you do not, it is a product idea served on a plate."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: search term, 2: number of searches.
#: includes/insights.php:302
#, php-format
msgid "“%1$s” · %2$s searches"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:303
msgid "Type the term in your own search box and look at what comes out."
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:313
msgid "A whole country visits without ever buying"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:314
msgid "At least a tenth of the visits come from a country that never orders. Sometimes it is simply that you do not deliver there — then the visits are wasted and the message could say so earlier. Sometimes a payment method, a currency or a language is missing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:317
msgid "Check the shipping zones and payment methods available for this country in WooCommerce."
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:334
msgid "Campaigns run, but nothing remembers them past the visit"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:335
msgid "Without the attribution memory, an order is only credited to a campaign if it happens during the very visit that came from it. Someone who clicks today and buys tomorrow counts as direct — campaign figures end up lower than reality."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %1$s: number of tagged visits.
#: includes/insights.php:337
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s tagged visits over the period · attribution memory off"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:338
msgid "Enable the attribution memory in Settings → Privacy if a small origin cookie is acceptable for your store."
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:401
#: includes/insights.php:446
msgid "Leads worth checking"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:402
msgid "Computed automatically from the period’s figures. They point at things to look at — they prove nothing, and they do not replace a proper analysis of your store."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: measured visits, 2: visits needed.
#: includes/insights.php:412
#, php-format
msgid "Not enough data yet: %1$s visits measured over this period, %2$s needed before a lead means anything. Come back later, or widen the period."
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:417
msgid "Nothing stands out over this period. That is good news — or a sign that the period is too short to tell."
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:427
msgid "Worth doing:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:432
msgid "Take these with a pinch of salt: a rule sees a correlation, never a cause. It knows nothing of the season, your margins, your stock or the promotion running this week."
msgstr ""

#: includes/insights.php:446
msgid "Simple rules applied to the period’s figures: a page that loses its visitors, a source that never converts, a product viewed a lot and never added to the cart. Each lead shows the numbers that triggered it, so you can disagree with it."
msgstr ""

